6. NAVIGATION CART BADGE: STRICT 99+ DISPLAY LIMIT
==================================================

The navigation bar's cart indicator must follow a strict display rule.

The actual cart quantity may continue increasing.

However, the navigation cart badge must NEVER display a number greater than 99.

Required behavior:

| Actual Cart Units | Navigation Badge |
|-------------------|------------------|
| 0 | Hidden or existing empty state |
| 1 | 1 |
| 10 | 10 |
| 25 | 25 |
| 50 | 50 |
| 98 | 98 |
| 99 | 99 |
| 100 | 99+ |
| 150 | 99+ |
| 200 | 99+ |
| 500 | 99+ |
| 1,000 | 99+ |

Implementation rule:

If totalCartUnits <= 99:

Display the actual number.

If totalCartUnits > 99:

Display exactly:

99+

The navigation badge must never display:

100, 150, 200, 500, or 1000.

IMPORTANT:

This is a presentation-only restriction.

Do not limit the actual cart quantity to 99.

Do not truncate database quantities.

Do not change the actual cart state to 99.

The actual cart quantity must remain accurate.

--------------------------------------------------
A. BADGE RESPONSIVENESS
--------------------------------------------------

The 99+ badge must:

- Remain visually balanced.
- Fit properly beside the cart icon.
- Work on mobile and desktop.
- Avoid breaking navigation spacing.
- Maintain readable typography.
- Avoid layout shifts.

